Both apps under src/ are deliberately parallel in shape: each owns its own
package.json, Dockerfile, .dockerignore, and tests/{unit,integration}/.
Nothing app-specific lives outside src/backend/ or src/frontend/ -- the
root package.json exists only to make `npm run dev`/`setup` convenient from
one place, and root-level files (docker-compose.yml, render.yaml, scripts/,
docs/) are cross-cutting tooling/documentation, not part of either app.
